    {
      "id": "chat-ada-stadium-empty",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "reply",
      "trigger": null,
      "title": null,
      "text": "Empty space. Mostly just empty space!\n\nThat is why an atom is so much bigger than its nucleus.\n\nThings still feel solid, because the electrons in them push back on the electrons in your hand.",
      "pose": "proud",
      "replies": [
        {
          "label": "mind-blown",
          "type": "emoji",
          "next": "chat-ada-stadium-end"
        },
        {
          "label": "star",
          "type": "emoji"
        }
      ],
      "position": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-ada-stadium-end",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "sign_off",
      "trigger": null,
      "title": null,
      "text": "That was the marble in the stadium.\n\nCome back to it any time. I will tell it again.",
      "pose": "proud",
      "replies": [],
      "position": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-ada-stadium-why",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "reply",
      "trigger": null,
      "title": null,
      "text": "Good thing to wonder about.\n\nThe nucleus is made of protons and neutrons, packed tightly together.\n\nThe electrons are tiny and fast, and they keep their distance from it.",
      "pose": "explain",
      "replies": [
        {
          "label": "So what is between?",
          "next": "chat-ada-stadium-empty"
        },
        {
          "label": "Open the nucleus in AtomDex",
          "action": {
            "screen": "entry",
            "id": "nucleus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "position": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-ada-stadium-wow",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "reply",
      "trigger": null,
      "title": null,
      "text": "Really. Almost all of the atom's mass is packed into that marble.\n\nThe electrons are far lighter, and they are out near the seats.\n\nSo what is in between?",
      "pose": "proud",
      "replies": [
        {
          "label": "Nothing at all?",
          "next": "chat-ada-stadium-empty"
        },
        {
          "label": "Where are the electrons?",
          "next": "chat-ada-stadium-why"
        }
      ],
      "position": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-ada-up-stadium",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "unprompted",
      "trigger": "lessons_completed:3",
      "title": "A marble in a stadium",
      "text": "Hi! Ada here. I have to tell you something that still surprises me.\n\nPicture an atom blown up until it is as big as a football stadium.\n\nHow big would its nucleus be, right in the middle? About the size of a marble.",
      "pose": "explain",
      "replies": [
        {
          "label": "wow",
